On Sunday, May 5, 2013 9:32:46 AM UTC-4, Yves Rosseel wrote:
> On 05/04/2013 08:45 PM, Terrence Jorgensen wrote:
> > Hi Bill,
> >
> > There are no problems with your model specification or your call to
> > Amelia.  The reason you see the warnings is because it is a saturated
> > model.  Saturated models have a chi-squared value of zero, which is all
> > well and good, but they also have zero degrees of freedom.  So when
> > runMI() tries to combine the chi-squared values, it is making a call to
> > calculate the probabilities (/p/ values) of observing the chi-squared or
> > /F/ value when /df/ = 0, which is undefined.  However, notice that all
> > the warnings concern calls to pf() and pchisq(), so that is the only
> > issue.  You models were estimated and parameters combined successfully:
>
> Agreed. And adding the option chi="none" gets rid of all the warnings:
>
> out.mi <- runMI(employReg3, data=mf_merge$imputations, fun="sem",
> chi="none")
>
> Perhaps runMI() should detect this case (df=0) and switch to chi="none"
> automatically... and that is why I CCed this to Sunthud ;-)
>
> Yves.
>
>

