Dear Lavaan-users,

I recently started using lavaan, but encounter some convergence problems when trying to fit my models.

I have a dataset with scores between 0 and 5 of 783 participants on 15 variables. The scores are the sum of 5 very similar items (with correct=1, incorrect=0) on 15 different subtests. I tread the scores as ordered given the limited range of possible values and skewness of the data.

I would like to do a confirmatory factor analyses and have some alternative models to test (I’ll  validate the final model on a different data sample). Below, I show the model specifications. As you can see, not all models use all variables, so for each model I take a subsample of the data (mod1: 8 variables; mod2 and mod3: 13 variables).

mod1 <- 'motion  =~ t6 + t9  + t11 + t12

         meaning =~ t9 + t10 + t13 + t15

         color   =~ t5 + t10 + t13 + t15'

mod2 <- 'grouping      =~ t2 + t3 + t6 + t7 + t8 + t9 + t11 + t12 + t14

        segmentation  =~ t3 + t5 + t6 + t7 + t11 + t14 + t15

        figure_ground =~ t3 + t5 + t6 + t7

        shape         =~ t1 + t3 + t4 + t5 + t6 + t7 + t8 + t14'

mod3 <- 'spatial_relations =~ t1 + t2 + t3 + t4 + t5 + t7 + t8 + t9 + t10 + t11 +t14

        fine_details      =~ t1 + t2 + t3 + t4 + t7 + t8

        cue_invariance    =~ t3 + t5 + t6 + t7 + t8

        shape_invariance  =~ t1 + t3 + t7 +t8'

I estimate the models with the following statements:

fit1<-cfa(mod1, data=cfa_subtests_data1, ordered=c("t5","t6","t9","t10","t11","t12","t13","t15") )

fit2<-cfa(mod2, data=cfa_subtests_data2, ordered=c("t1","t2", "t3", "t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t11","t12","t14","t15") )

fit3<-cfa(mod3, data=cfa_subtests_data3, ordered=c("t1","t2", "t3", "t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t10","t11","t14") )

None of these models reach convergence. I always get this error message:

lavaan WARNING: model has NOT converged!

Simplifying  the models by removing one factor of by changing the latent variable definition does not seem to help. At the best I get my estimates but with this warning:
lavaan WARNING: covariance matrix of latent variables is not positive definite

Is this a problem in my model specifications or is my model not identifiable? How could this be solved?

Also, a couple of months ago I performed a similar analysis with lavaan 0.5-11 and this worked fine, but since I updated to lavaan 0.5-12 I get a warning that the covariance matrix is not positive definite with exactly the same code. Could this be related to the convergence problems I experience now? My code for the this similar analysis is:

cfamodel1 <- 'Grouping  =~ t2 + t6 + t9 + t11+ t12

            Figureground=~ t3 + t5 + t7 +t8 + t13 + t15

GlobalLocal =~ t10 + t14

ShapeDiscr  =~ t1 + t4'

fit <- cfa(cfamodel1, data=subtest.data, ordered=c('t1', 't2', 't3', 't4', 't5', 't6', 't7', 't8', t9', 't10', 't11', 't12', 't13','t14', 't15'))

I use R 2.15 with lavaan 0.5-12. If you need any other information, please let me know.

Any help would he highly appreciated.

Kind regards,

Kathleen Vancleef

