That is because lavaanify needs many more options. If you are using
'sem', try

dyad.model3a = lavaanify(dyad.model2, constraints = 'C == D', auto=TRUE)

>>dyad.fit3a = sem(dyad.model3a, fixed.x = F, sample.cov = dom.cov,
> sample.nobs = 112)

But why do you need the lavaanify() function? You could call sem()
directly like this:

dyad.fit3a = sem(dyad.model3a, fixed.x = F, sample.cov = dom.cov,

sample.nobs = 112, constraints = 'C == D')

Yves.

