Hi all,

Two questions. At least one is silly, but was up late last night unable to figure it out. Im running a multifactor cfa with purely dichotomous indicators, using the ordered statement.

1) how can I extract the indicator error term variances? I imagine I use inspect somehow but couldn't figure it out. I want to calculate composite reliability and average variance extracted, and I have many indicators so I'd like to dump the variances into a vector to manipulate.

2) my model gives me a warning message that the matrix isn't positive semi definite, and indeed I have eigenvalues just under zero. I still get all the estimates and statistics reported. Is it dangerous to work with the results? The model has decent theoretical backing, I suspect the problem is in part due to small sample size (around 100) and a lot of indicators (around 60, with 5 factors) (note I have no crossloadings in my model). I'm probably doing something idiotic so feel free to chastise if necessary!

From u3fe90052fbf2f899 at groups.google.com  Thu May 30 03:13:19 2013
