To follow up on my earlier post: if you have multiple groups, you can use:

ov.names <- lavNames(fit, "ov")
PE <- parameterEstimates(fit)

ev1 <- PE[ PE$op=="~~" & PE$lhs %in% ov.names & PE$lhs == PE$rhs &
PE$group == 1,"est"]
ev2 <- PE[ PE$op=="~~" & PE$lhs %in% ov.names & PE$lhs == PE$rhs &
PE$group == 2,"est"]

etc.

> 2) my model gives me a warning message that the matrix isn't positive
> semi definite, and indeed I have eigenvalues just under zero. I still
> get all the estimates and statistics reported. Is it dangerous to
> work with the results?

Quite frankly, I'm not sure. I have been trying to find some literature
on this, but could not find any. I did notice that some commercial
programs seem to be slighly less strict, in the sense that they do not
show a warning if the negative eigenvalue is very close to zero. So
perhaps, lavaan is too strict here.

Yves.

